author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The classifier distinguishes prose compounds from evidence-backed issue identifiers without maintaining an unbounded dictionary; negative controls retain detection for real uppercase and configured code formats; validation output explains the evidence and recovery path; focused tests cover Match-3, Covid-19, Wi-Fi-6, real codes, mixed case, body evidence, and configured formats; the full validation and 100 percent coverage gates pass."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1118
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Create two unrelated items whose titles contain the same natural-language word-number token such as Match-3, then run pm validate --check-metadata."
expected_result: Natural-language compounds are not classified as logical issue codes; true structured issue codes and genuine collisions remain detected with actionable evidence.
actual_result: The generic title regex groups unrelated prose tokens as issue codes and recommends dishonest renames or merges.
